infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title A process does not choose when it dies
  desc Five independent triggers fire all day — and every one ends the same way: the orchestrator signals stop, then force-kills if you linger.
  lists
    - label Rolling deploy
      desc Every release replaces every instance; the old pod is signalled the moment the new one is ready.
    - label Autoscaler scale-down
      desc Traffic drops, the autoscaler removes capacity, and your instance is the one chosen to go.
    - label Node drain
      desc A node is cordoned for maintenance or upgrade; every pod on it is evicted.
    - label Spot reclaim
      desc A cheaper spot/preemptible instance is reclaimed by the provider, often on seconds of notice.
    - label Crash-loop neighbor
      desc A failing co-located pod forces a reschedule that moves yours along with it.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
